     4	//! Cut out of `edit_clip.rs` in road map 5's E2, which owed it a rule about
     5	//! `video.motion` and found a 1171-line file, and cut HERE because a split
     6	//! is not a placement: every other op in `edit_clip.rs` decides where a
     7	//! clip sits or what it is made of, while this one has to decide what the
     8	//! SECOND clip inherits — its base props from the evaluation at the cut, so
     9	//! the join is invisible; the actions that had not finished, rebased to its
    10	//! own clip time, with a straddled one narrowed to the keys it animated;
    11	//! and, since E2, the halves of a preset anchored to the clip's two ends.
    12	//! The cursor's `smoothing` and `hide_idle` are the one exception to "the
    13	//! evaluation at the cut": the second half keeps the original's base values
    14	//! (spec §11 CU-30).
    15	//! That inheritance question is the whole of this module and appears
    16	//! nowhere else in the crate.
    17	//!
    18	//! Every splitter in the crate routes here — `split_clips`,
    19	//! `split_under_playhead`, `clear_range` (so `ripple_delete_range(s)` and
    20	//! `lift_range`), `insert_clip`, `overwrite_clip`, `freeze_frame` and
    21	//! `keep_range` — so a rule stated once is a rule they all obey. It is a
    22	//! free function taking `&mut Project` rather than a `Project` method for
